step Fishing 175-225: Alterac Mountains
  when zone "Alterac Mountains"
  zone Alterac Mountains
  tip If you don't know Mithril Headed Trout yet, the arrow first takes you to its nearest seller. Fish the lake by the ruins of Alterac until Fishing 225 and cook what you catch as you go until Cooking 225: about 58% of catches are Raw Mithril Head Trout, so cook Mithril Headed Trout. Place a Basic Campfire Kit beside the water (one every 5 minutes) and empty your bags into the fire; any fish recipe you know counts toward the Cooking target. The Raw Mithril Head Trout line counts the fish you still need for Cooking 225 (about 52 from Cooking 175) and drops as your Cooking rises; once your bags hold that many, stop fishing and cook. That is roughly 90 casts here, about 30 minutes. Save about 3g 20s for Fishing 225: the Spotted Yellowtail and Filet of Redgill recipes cost 1g 60s each, plus the Alterac Swiss for the Artisan Cooking quest.
  learn 20916 nearest
  skill Fishing 225
  collect 8365 x52 anywhere optional
  craft 20916 until 225
  goto 30.4,35.2 "Alterac lake" r 25 optional

step Buy Recipe: Rockscale Cod
  when zone "Stranglethorn Vale"
  when !knows 7828
  tip Recipe: Rockscale Cod is an item a vendor sells, usually the fishing supplier. The arrow points at the nearest seller: buy it, then right-click it in your bags to learn it.
  buy 6369 x1 nearest
  learn 7828

step Fishing 175-225: Stranglethorn Vale
  when zone "Stranglethorn Vale"
  zone Stranglethorn Vale
  tip If you don't know Rockscale Cod yet, the arrow first takes you to its nearest seller. Fish the bay under Booty Bay until Fishing 225 and cook what you catch as you go until Cooking 225: about 55% of catches are Raw Rockscale Cod, so cook Rockscale Cod. Place a Basic Campfire Kit beside the water (one every 5 minutes) and empty your bags into the fire; any fish recipe you know counts toward the Cooking target. The Raw Rockscale Cod line counts the fish you still need for Cooking 225 (about 95 from Cooking 175) and drops as your Cooking rises; once your bags hold that many, stop fishing and cook. That is roughly 180 casts here, about 55 minutes. Away from this coast, Stranglethorn Vale's inland water gives Raw Mithril Head Trout (about 58% of catches), and Cooking 175-225 takes only about 52 of those: learn Mithril Headed Trout and fish there if you know a spot. Save about 3g 20s for Fishing 225: the Spotted Yellowtail and Filet of Redgill recipes cost 1g 60s each, plus the Alterac Swiss for the Artisan Cooking quest.
  learn 7828 nearest
  skill Fishing 225
  collect 6362 x95 anywhere optional
  craft 7828 until 225
  goto 27.42,77.16 "Booty Bay docks" r 25 optional

